# A widget of several clauses with a plain pair as its result applied, above the line that
# gives it, to a building `if`'s late plain result, its pair taken apart by a tuple
# pattern (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles": any line may use any name the
# block binds, and "the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else";
# ch. 8: `<-` builds the child and binds its plain result, here by a pattern; ruling TC).
# Nothing here is a cycle. Green on keep-B: a probe of `DeferredLine`'s refusal "gives a
# plain result of its own that no name binds", which a tuple pattern does not reach.
# Written by Claude (sweep-4, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Wide: fn Nat -> @((Nat, Nat))
fn @Wide 10:
    Ui.Label($text=$"ten")
    @ ((1, 2))
fn @Wide k:
    @ ((3, 4))

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    ((a, b)) <- @Wide n                                                # 0 when n is 10
    Ui.Label($text=$"wide {a} {b}")                                    # 1, or 0
    n <- if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"loud")                                        # 2
        @ 10
    else:
        @ 20
